PATCH 303: reconstruct the MGAVIDEO cockpit-sprite BLIT CHAIN (279d dispatcher + 27de RLE blitter) +
expose the 260c cx output, reached 209e -> 7896 (patch 301) -> c6bc -> 279d -> 260c -> 27de on the AZER1
ACCEPT mission path.  Both 279d/27de were base-lost by Ghidra (host-ptr derefs of the sprite record /
the VGA dest / the DGROUP rowtable) -> SIGSEGV; reconstructed as faithful SEGMENTED transliterations
(uint16 wrap keeps every cursor in its 64KB segment -> memory-safe).  asm-verified vs
re_out/fist_mga_image.bin:

  260c (0x260c): publish m_260c_cx = iVar4 (= -(hdr>>9), the sprite top-row offset the asm computes as
                 `mov cl,ah; xor ch,ch; neg cx`) for 279d's ZF=0 blit path.  No behaviour change to the
                 existing 260c callers (26a1/294d/... in the menus) -- an added static store only.
  279d (0x279d): sprite blit dispatcher (sibling of 294d/patch 136): ax=sprite dir offset, bx=position;
                 260c resolves ES:SI (m_260c_recoff) + clip + CF/ZF; ZF=1 -> 2d6d coord transform + 27de,
                 ZF=0 -> 27de(...,cx).  Use the 260c shim statics, not the dropped param.
  27de (0x27de): run-length sprite blitter -- src=DS:SI=m_260c_recseg:recoff, dest=ES:di (ES=word[c724],
                 di=rowtable[param_4]+col-1 decreasing 1/px), stride=word[c724+4]; header word[si-4] =
                 run length / row count, word[si-2]==2 selects the skip/count RLE encoding.

MISSION-PATH ONLY (dispatched only by the cockpit paint chain; 279d/27de were unreached/crashing before)
-> behaviour-neutral for the 19 verify flows.

